<!-- panda-rules-start -->
## PandaFilter Token Optimization Rules

When running shell commands, prefix the following commands with `/usr/local/bin/panda run` to enable
automatic output compression and token savings:

- `git` operations: `/usr/local/bin/panda run git status`, `/usr/local/bin/panda run git diff`, etc.
- `cargo` builds: `/usr/local/bin/panda run cargo build`, `/usr/local/bin/panda run cargo test`
- `docker` / `kubectl` / `terraform` commands
- Test runners: `/usr/local/bin/panda run npm test`, `/usr/local/bin/panda run pytest`, `/usr/local/bin/panda run go test ./...`
- Linters: `/usr/local/bin/panda run eslint .`, `/usr/local/bin/panda run mypy .`

When you see output containing `[N matching lines collapsed — panda expand ID]`, you can
retrieve the original lines with `/usr/local/bin/panda expand ID`.
<!-- panda-rules-end -->
